  ('8b6e21c6-5c02-5469-8905-555a276a17e8', 'WBC-CAP-DC-048', 2, 'Important', 'L2', 1, 'Structured evidence handling; bounded judgement; escalation discipline; role-specific coordination'),
  ('57a0aaf5-0030-56d5-b2b5-d1c25c932dd1', 'LFA-CAP-SUB001-SAMPLE', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate-to-high openness to visual and technical correction, patient attention to detail, steady emotional regulation, and collaborative agreeableness. This profile is especially important under sample revision cycles and approval deadlines in finished leather shade, finish, recipe, and buyer sample approval. Observable work demands: Compares sample requirements before recording corrections using shade matching card; tannery recipe sheet; drum processing log; identifies shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to leather technologist, tannery QA, production owner, or buyer coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: sample revision cycles and approval deadlines, particularly when shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; the wider environment also includes shade drift, finish mismatch, chemical or traceability evidence gaps, ETP record incompleteness, and buyer sample deadlines.'),
  ('47cd9e4c-1b47-5075-a0b1-533f94910d5d', 'LFA-CAP-SUB001-SAMPLE', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate-to-high openness to visual and technical correction, patient attention to detail, steady emotional regulation, and collaborative agreeableness. This profile is especially important under sample revision cycles and approval deadlines in finished leather shade, finish, recipe, and buyer sample approval. Observable work demands: Compares sample requirements before recording corrections using shade matching card; tannery recipe sheet; drum processing log; identifies shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to leather technologist, tannery QA, production owner, or buyer coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: sample revision cycles and approval deadlines, particularly when shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; the wider environment also includes shade drift, finish mismatch, chemical or traceability evidence gaps, ETP record incompleteness, and buyer sample deadlines.'),
  ('2fe6c0bc-5239-58be-81cd-a9db0cdd87ed', 'LFA-CAP-SUB001-SAMPLE', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate-to-high openness to visual and technical correction, patient attention to detail, steady emotional regulation, and collaborative agreeableness. This profile is especially important under sample revision cycles and approval deadlines in finished leather shade, finish, recipe, and buyer sample approval. Observable work demands: Compares sample requirements before recording corrections using shade matching card; tannery recipe sheet; drum processing log; identifies shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to leather technologist, tannery QA, production owner, or buyer coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: sample revision cycles and approval deadlines, particularly when shade variation, thickness deviation, surface defect, finish mismatch, or missing lot identity; the wider environment also includes shade drift, finish mismatch, chemical or traceability evidence gaps, ETP record incompleteness, and buyer sample deadlines.'),
  ('309c7a5b-3490-58c6-88c9-c700e7c26dfd', 'LFA-CAP-SUB001-MERCH', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate extraversion, collaborative agreeableness, steady emotional regulation, and openness to buyer or supplier feedback. This profile is especially important under buyer response, supplier follow-up, order accuracy, and shipment cut-off timing in finished leather buyer comment, order documentation, and export handoff. Observable work demands: Closes buyer, supplier, order, and shipment actions with traceable evidence using shade matching card; ETP daily log; chemical inventory register; identifies unclosed buyer comment, wrong shade/order reference, missing test evidence, or incomplete export document; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to finished leather merchandiser, QA, compliance owner, or export documentation coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: buyer response, supplier follow-up, order accuracy, and shipment cut-off timing, particularly when unclosed buyer comment, wrong shade/order reference, missing test evidence, or incomplete export document; the wider environment also includes shade drift, finish mismatch, chemical or traceability evidence gaps, ETP record incompleteness, and buyer sample deadlines.'),
