  ('0867d5c5-4861-5023-a1d6-be57c6a5d493', 'LFA-CAP-SUB001-QA', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'Very high conscientiousness, evidence-oriented openness, low impulsivity, stable stress response, and sufficient assertiveness to escalate nonconformance. This profile is especially important under inspection consistency, hold pressure, corrective-action closure, and shipment timing in leather lab testing, traceability, etp, and restricted substance release. Observable work demands: Applies inspection criteria consistently before making a hold or release recommendation using shade matching card; ETP daily log; chemical inventory register; identifies failed test result, traceability break, chemical/MRSL gap, ETP evidence gap, or shade mismatch; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to QA manager, compliance owner, buyer coordinator, or production owner without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: inspection consistency, hold pressure, corrective-action closure, and shipment timing, particularly when failed test result, traceability break, chemical/MRSL gap, ETP evidence gap, or shade mismatch; the wider environment also includes shade drift, finish mismatch, chemical or traceability evidence gaps, ETP record incompleteness, and buyer sample deadlines.'),
