  ('df53ffdd-1eff-5e71-952b-eb84b9c75d00', 'LFA-CAP-SUB002-QA', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'Very high conscientiousness, evidence-oriented openness, low impulsivity, stable stress response, and sufficient assertiveness to escalate nonconformance. This profile is especially important under inspection consistency, hold pressure, corrective-action closure, and shipment timing in footwear aql, bis/qco, fit, bond, defect, and shipment release. Observable work demands: Applies inspection criteria consistently before making a hold or release recommendation using AQL shoe inspection sheet; BIS QCO checklist; lasting and sole bonding log; identifies critical defect, failed bond, fit issue, QCO evidence gap, or packaging/labeling error; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to QA manager, production supervisor, merchandising, or compliance executive without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: inspection consistency, hold pressure, corrective-action closure, and shipment timing, particularly when critical defect, failed bond, fit issue, QCO evidence gap, or packaging/labeling error; the wider environment also includes WIP delay, rework accumulation, bond or fit failure, BIS/QCO evidence gaps, buyer corrections, and shipment cut-off dates.'),
  ('df53ffdd-1eff-5e71-952b-eb84b9c75d00', 'LFA-CAP-SUB002-COMPLIANCE', 2, 'Important', 'L5', 5, 'Very high conscientiousness, low impulsivity, stable stress response, rule discipline, and willingness to challenge unsupported claims. This profile is especially important under BIS/QCO or buyer-rule evidence gaps, QA holds, and shipment-release pressure in footwear bis/qco and buyer compliance evidence support. Observable work demands: Matches each compliance statement to the applicable checklist and supporting evidence using BIS QCO checklist; AQL shoe inspection sheet; lasting and sole bonding log; identifies missing BIS/QCO evidence, failed AQL status, bond failure, or unsupported buyer compliance claim; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to QA manager, compliance executive, or buyer coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: BIS/QCO or buyer-rule evidence gaps, QA holds, and shipment-release pressure, particularly when missing BIS/QCO evidence, failed AQL status, bond failure, or unsupported buyer compliance claim; the wider environment also includes WIP delay, rework accumulation, bond or fit failure, BIS/QCO evidence gaps, buyer corrections, and shipment cut-off dates.'),
