  ('8ab41bb3-52eb-552e-824b-a5691eb48da0', 'LFA-CAP-SUB003-SAMPLE', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate-to-high openness to visual and technical correction, patient attention to detail, steady emotional regulation, and collaborative agreeableness. This profile is especially important under sample revision cycles and approval deadlines in polymeric footwear material, mould, outsole, and sample approval. Observable work demands: Compares sample requirements before recording corrections using mould setup card; compound mixing sheet; outsole test record; identifies wrong material grade, mould mismatch, outsole size variation, finish defect, or unclosed sample correction; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to mould development technician, sample coordinator, QA, or buyer coordinator without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: sample revision cycles and approval deadlines, particularly when wrong material grade, mould mismatch, outsole size variation, finish defect, or unclosed sample correction; the wider environment also includes material-mix deviation, mould damage, curing-cycle variation, QCO nonconformance, batch holds, and dispatch deadlines.'),
