  ('c47ac368-96ea-5505-9200-677c38e87d32', 'LFA-CAP-SUB007-SAMPLE', 1, 'Core', 'L5', 5, 'High conscientiousness, moderate-to-high openness to visual and technical correction, patient attention to detail, steady emotional regulation, and collaborative agreeableness. This profile is especially important under sample revision cycles and approval deadlines in upper, component bom, insole/outsole, supplier sample, and buyer component approval. Observable work demands: Compares sample requirements before recording corrections using component BOM; upper stitching plan; bonding test record; identifies wrong component specification, supplier sample mismatch, bonding issue, size/spec deviation, or unclosed buyer comment; records the evidence trail; and routes the case to upper developer, supplier sample coordinator, component QA, or buyer handoff owner without claiming final approval, certification, audit, legal, buyer sign-off, or release authority. Workplace pressure: sample revision cycles and approval deadlines, particularly when wrong component specification, supplier sample mismatch, bonding issue, size/spec deviation, or unclosed buyer comment; the wider environment also includes supplier mismatch, bonding or stitch failure, incorrect BOM or batch card, dispatch-label errors, and buyer handoff delays.'),
